-- title:
--   Fractional ideals away from a finite set are generated by the remaining primes
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field and let $S$ be a finite set of nonzero primes of $\mathcal O_K$. In the group of invertible fractional ideals, let
--
--   $$
--   I^S=\{I:v_{\mathfrak p}(I)=0\text{ for every }\mathfrak p\in S\},
--   $$
--
--   where $v_{\mathfrak p}(I)$ is the prime-ideal exponent. Then
--
--   $$
--   I^S=\langle\mathfrak p:\mathfrak p\notin S\rangle.
--   $$
--
--   This gives generators for the ideal group underlying coprimality and ray class constructions.
--
